  "verbalization": "Bleomycin is linked to NCI-H2196 through a series of molecular interactions, with the core mechanism involving the targeting of a specific compound by bleomycin. The evidence suggests that bleomycin acts as a target for multiple entities, including A388 and HCE-T, which in turn target the compound [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate. This compound is ultimately targeted by NCI-H2196, indicating a chain of molecular interactions where bleomycin influences the activity of a downstream molecule that interacts with NCI-H2196. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which bleomycin may modulate the function of NCI-H2196, possibly through the inhibition of a key enzyme or the disruption of a specific biochemical pathway. The evidence supports a role for bleomycin in the regulation of NCI-H2196, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
